### Gradle Patch ###
# Java heap dump
*.hprof

# End of https://www.toptal.com/developers/gitignore/api/git,intellij+all,vue,vuejs,gradle,kotlin,macos,windows,linux
.venv/

# Retained artifacts of a `scripts/run_web_e2e.py` run: per-boot backend logs, per-boot config-secret KEK files
# and the per-suite canary files the wire-assertion sweep reads (ADR 0053). Local debugging output — a boot log
# holds real instance state and a canary file holds the plaintext a suite sealed, so neither is committable.
.e2e-out/

# The server-managed config-secret KEK file (ADR 0050 amendment). Generated on first start at the default path
# (relative to the process CWD); it is a real secret and must never be committed. Operators keep it on a persisted
# volume; a local dev/quarkusDev run drops one here.
config-secret.key
**/config-secret.key

# graphify's build output (knowledge graph, report, caches). Derived from the tree on demand and rebuilt by
# `/graphify --update`, so it is never a source of truth — and it embeds absolute local paths. `_SKIP_DIRS` in
# graphify's own detector already ignores it, so the graph never ingests itself; this only keeps it out of git.
graphify-out/
# The docs site's generated content types (ADR 0087), rebuilt by `astro check` / `astro build`.
site/.astro/

# The root launcher's per-checkout ports (settings.gradle.kts): a worktree's own, never shared.
/local.properties
